 :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86c08b66-dfaf-5856-9af2-f0ab92ff0c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463987} :answer-field/id #uuid "349fc697-8240-52e6-8d87-9502507de6df" :answer-field/key "$[0,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464927}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3d989e0b-f261-53e6-891f-e36529fecf99" :question/math-academy-id "q-131180" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-1, & x<-1 \\\\ {x}^{3}, & -1\\le x<1 \\\\ 1, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nSo, let's check whether the function is continuous on each of the intervals.\n\n- The interval $(-1,1)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- Now, consider $[-2,0].$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -{1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}(-1)=-1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to -{1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}({x}^{3})=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the limits from the left and from the right of $x=-1$ are the same. Hence, $f(x)$ is continuous on the interval $[-2,0],$ and the extreme value theorem is applicable on this interval.\n\n- Finally, consider $[0,2].$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}({x}^{3})=1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}(1)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the limits from the left and from the right of $x=1$ are the same. Hence, $f(x)$ is continuous on the interval $[0,2],$ and the extreme value theorem is applicable on this interval.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is $[-2,0]$; $[0,2]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Divergence" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049459 :topic/id #uuid "f6fd4776-56f0-5112-9cdc-83e344004d93" :topic/math-academy-id 2131 :topic/title "The Divergence of a Vector Field"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b57f211c-710e-5cdf-9dc0-86b8aefe98af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437824} {:answer/id #uuid "b929d2fd-0b41-5609-a3b0-fa86b7e1dd4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b57f211c-710e-5cdf-9dc0-86b8aefe98af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437824} :answer-field/id #uuid "776c15bd-b517-5de8-bd02-bce5d321a9e0" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438941} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7621cbc-9096-553a-84ec-b2f2f4e2f4bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437826} {:answer/id #uuid "311543c2-d6ee-5d2f-a97e-a5b65483a921" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "311543c2-d6ee-5d2f-a97e-a5b65483a921" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437827} :answer-field/id #uuid "70f009df-f6c2-5904-a0e1-25a9ae42998b" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438942} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "968b9198-d75a-5f15-96eb-a2deea0b5e3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437828} {:answer/id #uuid "a2060c37-7ca9-58ba-a491-191632fc1573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "968b9198-d75a-5f15-96eb-a2deea0b5e3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437828} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c5ab0f1-4f67-5325-afe4-5abf634a244d" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438943} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2879eacd-db77-5b78-ab2f-2988249602a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437830} {:answer/id #uuid "57da22cf-0696-5ee6-bc8a-520cb3a68dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2879eacd-db77-5b78-ab2f-2988249602a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437830} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ae32b58-4231-556f-87c0-2f75598b5de0" :answer-field/key "$F$ is solenoidal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "48d2c508-8f65-5677-91ea-4bbc2f84d34b" :question/math-academy-id "q-131192" :question/problem "![](images/e3/e30919dc7cc107bdda9872079b4dc0e59fe8e3e5767aa2d407b9d0af392803e0.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{div}\\,F>0$ is true, whereas statements $\\text{div}\\,F=0$ and $\\text{div}\\,F<0$ are false. Notice that the lengths of the vector's $y$-components increase as we move vertically away from the origin. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is solenoidal” is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{div}\\,F>0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266063 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Divergence" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049459 :topic/id #uuid "f6fd4776-56f0-5112-9cdc-83e344004d93" :topic/math-academy-id 2131 :topic/title "The Divergence of a Vector Field"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e94a2c2-3c82-5231-8b63-336e1f39ed5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437832} {:answer/id #uuid "73f8ff38-9d88-5841-a511-f2acede95070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73f8ff38-9d88-5841-a511-f2acede95070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437833} :answer-field/id #uuid "e61f3a78-17b9-5dc8-8814-0cc4b4a2ccae" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438945} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0116b48-f34e-5dd2-be8e-b3934161f541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437834} {:answer/id #uuid "d4bdeb0c-7d25-5346-865a-0cafac7b14d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0116b48-f34e-5dd2-be8e-b3934161f541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437834} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e71969a-fcaa-5b92-84fb-70734def355c" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438946} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f5fd46a-bab0-5a7c-95ba-10cde097fd6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437836} {:answer/id #uuid "95b4696f-fe0f-5b45-b776-8bdb7c506f5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f5fd46a-bab0-5a7c-95ba-10cde097fd6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437836} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5b8857e-16ee-534a-b0eb-3453864a2830" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438947} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1e09cb5-c71f-5894-835a-eeacd8a45f51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437838} {:answer/id #uuid "df4757fd-166f-51c8-80cd-31f6ea0ad7ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df4757fd-166f-51c8-80cd-31f6ea0ad7ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437839} :answer-field/id #uuid "67877ced-a15f-552a-9465-0ca79ff4d321" :answer-field/key "$F$ is solenoidal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4805821b-99fd-5b9d-aaa1-3579778dee2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-131193" :question/problem "![](images/24/243496443c3878c90fb67888add6c6ad6d3e69aa20ba24f42ee89d58a2742534.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{div}\\,F=0$ is true, whereas statements $\\text{div}\\,F>0$ and $\\text{div}\\,F<0$ are false. For any point $P,$ the sum of the inward-pointing vectors equals the sum of the outward-pointing vectors. Therefore, $F$ acts neither like a source nor a sink.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is solenoidal” is true. Since $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere, the vector field $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{div}\\,F=0$; “$F$ is solenoidal” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266069 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124480 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049723 :topic/id #uuid "0e15397e-6c32-508c-b6ea-90f1a9e5a237" :topic/math-academy-id 1904 :topic/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6e89ef2-9696-51d8-ae5e-a89095f5a24a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574295} {:answer/id #uuid "3bafb132-872b-57dd-bda5-82add9c3ccf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6e89ef2-9696-51d8-ae5e-a89095f5a24a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574295} :answer-field/id #uuid "47005496-403f-5dae-ade6-b866087cc701" :answer-field/key "Column 1: $\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/re