ven by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $2$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $2$nd and $3$rd columns." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049723 :topic/id #uuid "0e15397e-6c32-508c-b6ea-90f1a9e5a237" :topic/math-academy-id 1904 :topic/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"} :activity/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432890} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432891}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124480 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049723 :topic/id #uuid "0e15397e-6c32-508c-b6ea-90f1a9e5a237" :topic/math-academy-id 1904 :topic/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c82b71cc-9cf7-5a30-8e59-1c2c321c0689" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574301} {:answer/id #uuid "224634b6-ec97-5b92-a829-a96fc678221f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "224634b6-ec97-5b92-a829-a96fc678221f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/